  "body": "Currently we do `this.[[strategySize]] = size`, i.e. we destructure the strategy object into its component functions. This won't work for things like our CountQueuingStrategy and ByteLengthQueuingStrategy because they use methods, not functions.\n\nWe should retain the strategy object itself, and invoke the methods appropriately. We already have to (and do) handle the methods throwing, so in the same way we can handle them being non-functions. ES6's Invoke() operation will do the hard work for us.\n",
